ass_rate_neutral":0.5538,"def_epa_per_play":-0.09221},{"week":4,"opponent":"WAS","home":false,"pf":30.0,"pa":13.0,"off_snaps":64,"epa_per_play":-0.08585,"pass_rate":0.5625,"pass_rate_neutral":0.5763,"def_epa_per_play":-0.2498},{"week":5,"opponent":"PIT","home":false,"pf":22.0,"pa":34.0,"off_snaps":69,"epa_per_play":0.003426,"pass_rate":0.6522,"pass_rate_neutral":0.6,"def_epa_per_play":0.2431},{"week":6,"opponent":"TEN","home":true,"pf":20.0,"pa":26.0,"off_snaps":77,"epa_per_play":-0.1045,"pass_rate":0.6104,"pass_rate_neutral":0.56,"def_epa_per_play":-0.1473}],"comps":{"offense":[{"season":2023,"team":"GB","distance":0.4994,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Matt LaFleur"},{"season":2025,"team":"DAL","distance":0.5434,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Brian Schottenheimer"},{"season":2023,"team":"CLE","distance":0.5601,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Kevin Stefanski"},{"season":2022,"team":"GB","distance":0.599,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Matt LaFleur"},{"season":2025,"team":"LV","distance":0.6103,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Chip Kelly"}],"defense":[{"season":2022,"team":"NO","distance":0.2196,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Dennis Allen"},{"season":2025,"team":"TEN","distance":0.2678,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Dennard Wilson"},{"season":2022,"team":"HOU","distance":0.2906,"shared":4,"play_caller":null},{"season":2025,"team":"GB","distance":0.291,"shared":4,"play_caller":null},{"season":2024,"team":"NO","distance":0.2941,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Dennis Allen"}]},"overview":{"overview":"The Colts are 2-4 through week 6 of the 2026 season and have been outscored 164 to 144. The offense ranks 22nd in EPA per play and the defense 26th in EPA allowed, so neither side has stood out much yet. Their most distinctive trait is the 2nd lowest blitz rate in the league.","offense":"The Colts offense has been a little below average by EPA per play so far, and it has been much better running the ball than passing it. Their run and pass mix has stayed close to what game situations call for. Daniel Jones has run the passing game, with Josh Downs leading the team in targets.","defense":"The Colts defense has been well below average by EPA allowed per play so far. It has been much better against the pass than the run, ranking 22nd and 32nd. DeForest Buckner has led the way with 4 sacks. In terms of scheme, they have the 2nd lowest blitz rate in the league.","special":"The Colts have been about average in how often they go for it on fourth down. Their kickers have made 100% of field goals, which is the best in the league. On the roster side, they put an unusually large share of their salary cap into the secondary, about 29% of the money on the books. Their tight ends were among the oldest in the league.","players":"Daniel Jones has played nearly every snap at quarterback and thrown for 1,290 yards. Targets have been spread around, with Josh Downs and Keenan Allen leading a group where nobody has more than a fifth of the looks. Jonathan Taylor has handled most of the work in the backfield with 81% of the carries. On defense, DeForest Buckner leads the team with 4 sacks.","coaching":"Shane Steichen is calling the offense as head coach and Lou Anarumo is calling the defense. Their offense looks most like the 2023 Packers under Matt LaFleur and the 2025 Cowboys under Brian Schottenheimer. Their defense looks most like the 2022 Saints under Dennis Allen and the 2025 Titans under Dennard Wilson.","trends":"The offense went from 9th in EPA per play in 2025 to 22nd so far this season, a big step back. The defense moved from 16th in EPA allowed per play in 2025 to 26th so far this season, a big step back. The biggest change in approach was blitz rate, which went from 28% to 21%.","notes":"The 2026 pages are built from data that nflverse updates every week, so they will keep changing until the season ends. Personnel, formations, coverage and pressure numbers are missing for now because that data is only released after the season."}}